  "inertia_multiplier_finding": "The printed I column header reads 'mm4' with no multiplier. The sharp and filleted outlines give I = 1.20e9 (HKO300, sharp) / 1.196e9 (model) and 10.56e9 (sharp) / 10.53e9 (model, HKO600) mm4, so the missing multiplier is x10^9. I_mm4 above applies it; I_printed is verbatim.",
  "geometry_notes": [
   "Origin at mid-soffit, y up. The stem faces are straight lines from the theoretical root point (+/-135, 105) to the table top width B at y = H; 495 = 600 - 105 for the drawn HKO600 and 484 = B(HKO600), confirming this reading.",
   "990 is the width at the top of the 75 mm flange edge; the side face drafts 5 mm inward to the soffit (the '5' callout), with the dimensioned r=15 soffit corner.",
   "Flange edge: 30 mm flat at y = 75, then a 30 mm wide chamfer rising 13 mm to (435, 88); the flange top then rises 17 mm to the theoretical root at (135, 105).",
   "Stem/flange root fillet is drawn but undimensioned; ESTIMATE r = 15 mm (the dimensioned soffit radius; scaled drawing radius about 13 mm).",
   "The ø75/105 transverse holes at 250 mm centres are intermittent and excluded from the gross section.",
   "Published areas are three significant figures (+/-0.3%)."
  ],
  "pinned_discrepancies": {
   "HKO650": "Printed I = 13.27 (x10^9) is about 1.5% below the model value 13.47e9 and breaks the smooth HKO600/HKO700 progression (10.57, 13.27, 16.95); treated as a source error, pinned in tests."
  },
